From: Cepvor <cepvor@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 23:52:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AOSCOS: cmake: do not enable SVE/SVE2 from the build host on ARM64

FindSVE.cmake 和 FindSVE2.cmake 直接读构建机的 /proc/cpuinfo 判定是否启用
SVE，命中后通过 add_definitions() 追加 "-march=armv8-a+sve"。该参数出现在
编译命令行末尾，会覆盖发行版构建传入的 "-march=armv8-a" 基线，导致产物带
SVE 指令，在任何无 SVE 的 aarch64 机器上以 SIGILL 崩溃。

参照 0003 的做法，把探测结果放到显式开关之后，默认关闭；需要 SVE/SVE2 的
使用者仍可通过 -DENABLE_SVE=ON / -DENABLE_SVE2=ON 打开。

This commit is authored with assistance from AI/LLM:

- Model: Deepseek-v4.1-flash
- Platform: ZCode (self-adjusted, based on the open-source edition)
- Agent platform: none
- Prompt:
  在一台 8CX GEN3 设备上测试编解码，发现 x265 库有问题：ffmpeg -c:v libx265
  表现为静默失败，直接跑 x265 的 CLI 命令可以看到 Illegal instruction。

Assisted-by: DeepSeek <noreply@deepseek.com>
Signed-off-by: Cepvor <cepvor@qq.com>
---
 source/CMakeLists.txt | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/CMakeLists.txt b/source/CMakeLists.txt
index 0d703ab..48f6b37 100755
--- a/source/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/source/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -260,9 +260,22 @@ if(GCC)
         endif()
     endif()
 	if(ARM64 OR CROSS_COMPILE_ARM64)
+        # find_package() below probes the build host's CPU. A distribution
+        # build must not bake build-host features into the binary: a library
+        # built on an SVE-capable host crashes with SIGILL on machines that
+        # lack SVE. Honour an explicit ENABLE_SVE/ENABLE_SVE2 request instead.
+        option(ENABLE_SVE "Build SVE primitives (requires SVE on the target CPU)" OFF)
+        option(ENABLE_SVE2 "Build SVE2 primitives (requires SVE2 on the target CPU)" OFF)
         find_package(Neon)
         find_package(SVE)
         find_package(SVE2)
+        if(NOT ENABLE_SVE)
+            set(CPU_HAS_SVE 0)
+        endif()
+        if(NOT ENABLE_SVE2)
+            set(CPU_HAS_SVE2 0)
+            set(CROSS_COMPILE_SVE2 0)
+        endif()
         if(CPU_HAS_SVE2 OR CROSS_COMPILE_SVE2)
             message(STATUS "Found SVE2")
 	        set(ARM_ARGS -O3 -march=armv8-a+sve2 -fPIC -flax-vector-conversions)
